System Testing
____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
System Testing is a high-level testing phase performed after integration testing and before acceptance testing. 
It ensures the complete system works as intended in a production-like environment.

For system testing-- several environments are used:
QA environment, QC environment, UAT environment, TEsting environment, , own environment where we Test.

- It checks the overall functionality of an application with respect to customer requirements.
- System Testing is performed after Integration Testing.

System Testing mainly focuses on 4 main areas:  
GUI Testing
Usability Testing
Functional Testing*
Non-Functional Testing

*out of this funtionla testing is crucial and important testing area


Key Objectives
Functional verification – Confirm all features meet requirements.
Non-functional validation – Check performance, security, usability, and reliability.
End-to-end workflow – Validate business processes across modules.

Process
Test Environment Setup – Hardware, software, and network mimic production.
Test Case Design – Based on system requirements.
Execution & Defect Reporting – Compare actual vs expected outcomes.
Regression Testing – Ensure fixes don’t break existing functionality.
Retesting – Verify defect resolution.

Types of System Testing
Performance Testing – Speed & responsiveness.
Load Testing – Behavior under expected traffic.
Stress Testing – Extreme workload handling.
Security Testing – Vulnerability checks.

System testing involves functional and non-functional areas of application/product.
It mainly focuses on:
External interfaces
Multiprogram and complex functionalities
Security
Recovery
Performance
Operator and user’s smooth interaction with the system
Installability
Documentation
Usability
Load/Stress

Why System Testing
#1) It is very important to complete a full test cycle and ST is the stage where it is done.
#2) ST is performed in an environment that is similar to the production environment and hence stakeholders can get a good idea of the user’s reaction.
#3) It helps to minimize after-deployment troubleshooting and support calls.
#4) In this STLC stage, Application Architecture, and Business requirements both are tested.

This testing is very important, and it plays a significant role in delivering a quality product to the customer.

